@startuml sequence-communication-meeting
title CoreChain Communication - Video Meeting Lifecycle (LiveKit Integration)

actor "Manager" as Manager
actor "Employee" as Employee
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Communication\nService (Go)" as CommService
participant "JWT Auth\nMiddleware" as Auth
participant "MeetingHandler" as MeetingHandler
participant "MeetingService" as MeetingService
participant "LiveKitService" as LiveKit
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Kafka Broker" as Kafka
participant "LiveKit Server" as LiveKitServer
participant "Notification\nService (Go)" as NotifService

== Create Meeting (Manager Only) ==

Manager -> Client: Schedule new meeting
Client -> CommService: POST /meetings\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n{"title": "Team Sync",\n"description": "Weekly meeting",\n"invited_user_ids": ["user1", "user2"],\n"start_time": "2024-01-20T10:00:00Z"}

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth -> Auth: Validate JWT token\nExtract user_id and role
Auth --> CommService: user_id="mgr123"\nrole="MANAGER"

CommService -> MeetingHandler: CreateMeeting(request)
MeetingHandler -> MeetingHandler: Check role authorization

alt Role is not MANAGER or ADMIN
  MeetingHandler --> Client: 403 Forbidden\n{"error": "Manager role required"}
else Role authorized
  MeetingHandler -> MeetingService: CreateMeeting(ctx, title, description,\ncreatorID, invitedUserIDs, startTime)
  
  activate MeetingService
  MeetingService -> MeetingService: Generate unique\nroom name and meeting key
  
  MeetingService -> LiveKit: CreateRoom(roomName)
  LiveKit -> LiveKitServer: API call to create room\nwith configured settings
  LiveKitServer --> LiveKit: Room created\n{name, sid, metadata}
  LiveKit --> MeetingService: Room details
  
  MeetingService -> DB: INSERT INTO meetings\n(room_name, meeting_key, title,\ndescription, created_by,\ninvited_users, scheduled_time,\nstatus, livekit_room_sid)
  DB --> MeetingService: Meeting ID
  
  MeetingService -> Kafka: Publish event\ntopic: "meeting.created"\npayload: {meeting_id, title,\ninvited_users, start_time}
  Kafka --> MeetingService: Event published
  deactivate MeetingService
  
  MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Meeting record\n{id, room_name, meeting_key}
  MeetingHandler --> Client: 201 Created\n{"data": {"id": 789,\n"room_name": "room-abc123",\n"meeting_key": "key-xyz",\n"title": "Team Sync"}}
end

Client -> Manager: Meeting created

note right of Kafka
  **Async Notification**
  Kafka event triggers
  notifications to all
  invited participants
end note

== Kafka Consumer: Send Invitations ==

Kafka -> NotifService: Consume "meeting.created" event
NotifService -> DB: Query invited users'\nFCM tokens
DB --> NotifService: FCM tokens list
NotifService -> NotifService: Send FCM notification\nto each participant\n"You're invited to Team Sync"

note right of NotifService
  **Meeting Invitations**
  Separate Golang service
  handles push notifications
  to mobile devices
end note

== Join Meeting (Any Participant) ==

Employee -> Client: Join meeting notification
Client -> CommService: POST /meetings/join\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n{"room_name": "room-abc123",\n"meeting_key": "key-xyz"}

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth -> Auth: Validate JWT
Auth --> CommService: user_id="emp456"\nuser_name="John Doe"

CommService -> MeetingHandler: JoinMeeting(request)
MeetingHandler -> MeetingService: JoinMeeting(ctx, userID,\nuserName, roomName, meetingKey)

activate MeetingService
MeetingService -> DB: SELECT * FROM meetings\nWHERE room_name = 'room-abc123'\nAND meeting_key = 'key-xyz'
DB --> MeetingService: Meeting record

alt Meeting not found or invalid key
  MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Error: Invalid meeting
  MeetingHandler --> Client: 403 Forbidden\n{"error": "Invalid meeting credentials"}
else Meeting valid
  MeetingService -> MeetingService: Check if user is invited\n(user_id in invited_users)
  
  alt User not invited
    MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Error: Not authorized
    MeetingHandler --> Client: 403 Forbidden\n{"error": "You are not invited"}
  else User authorized
    MeetingService -> LiveKit: GenerateAccessToken\n(roomName, userID, userName)
    LiveKit -> LiveKit: Create JWT token\nwith LiveKit API credentials\nGrant: canPublish, canSubscribe
    LiveKit --> MeetingService: Access token
    
    MeetingService -> DB: INSERT INTO meeting_participants\n(meeting_id, user_id, joined_at,\nstatus='joined')
    DB --> MeetingService: Participant recorded
    
    MeetingService -> DB: UPDATE meetings\nSET status='active'\nWHERE id = meeting_id\nAND status='scheduled'
    DB --> MeetingService: Meeting activated
    
    deactivate MeetingService
    MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: {token, roomName, serverURL}
    MeetingHandler --> Client: 200 OK\n{"token": "eyJhbG...",\n"room_name": "room-abc123",\n"server_url": "wss://livekit.example.com"}
  end
end

alt Join successful
  Client -> LiveKitServer: Connect with access token\nWebRTC connection
  LiveKitServer --> Client: Connected to room\nAudio/Video streams
  Client -> Employee: In meeting (video/audio)
end

note right of LiveKit
  **LiveKit Integration**
  - JWT token generation
  - Room management
  - Participant permissions
  - WebRTC signaling
end note

== List My Meetings ==

Employee -> Client: View my meetings
Client -> CommService: GET /meetings/my\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth --> CommService: user_id authenticated

CommService -> MeetingHandler: ListMyMeetings(request)
MeetingHandler -> MeetingService: ListMyMeetings(ctx, userID)

MeetingService -> DB: SELECT * FROM meetings\nWHERE created_by = user_id\nOR user_id = ANY(invited_users)\nORDER BY scheduled_time DESC

DB --> MeetingService: Meetings list

MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Meetings array
MeetingHandler --> Client: 200 OK\n{"data": [meetings]}
Client -> Employee: Display meetings list

== End Meeting (Creator Only) ==

Manager -> Client: End meeting
Client -> CommService: POST /meetings/end\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n{"room_name": "room-abc123"}

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth --> CommService: user_id="mgr123"

CommService -> MeetingHandler: EndMeeting(request)
MeetingHandler -> MeetingService: EndMeeting(ctx, userID, roomName)

activate MeetingService
MeetingService -> DB: SELECT * FROM meetings\nWHERE room_name = 'room-abc123'
DB --> MeetingService: Meeting record

MeetingService -> MeetingService: Verify user is creator\n(created_by == user_id)

alt User is not creator
  MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Error: Not authorized
  MeetingHandler --> Client: 403 Forbidden\n{"error": "Only creator can end meeting"}
else User is creator
  MeetingService -> LiveKit: DeleteRoom(roomName)
  LiveKit -> LiveKitServer: API call to delete room\nDisconnect all participants
  LiveKitServer --> LiveKit: Room deleted
  LiveKit --> MeetingService: Success
  
  MeetingService -> DB: UPDATE meetings\nSET status='ended',\nended_at=NOW()\nWHERE room_name = 'room-abc123'
  DB --> MeetingService: Updated
  
  MeetingService -> Kafka: Publish event\ntopic: "meeting.ended"\npayload: {meeting_id, room_name}
  Kafka --> MeetingService: Event published
  
  deactivate MeetingService
  MeetingService --> MeetingHandler: Success
  MeetingHandler --> Client: 200 OK\n{"message": "Meeting ended successfully"}
end

Client -> Manager: Meeting ended
Client -> LiveKitServer: Disconnected
LiveKitServer -> Employee: Connection closed
Employee -> Client: Exits meeting

== Background Cleanup (DB Worker) ==

note over DB, Kafka
  **Scheduled Cleanup**
  DB Worker periodically checks for:
  - Abandoned meetings (active > 24 hours)
  - Expired scheduled meetings
  These are auto-ended and cleaned up
end note

@enduml
